# JSONL fixtures are byte-exact by design and must survive checkout untouched.
#
# Two things would otherwise silently break them, and both would turn a passing
# test into a test that cannot fail:
#
#   - CRLF conversion rewrites the 0x0A framing the adapters split on
#     (docs/design.md §4), and would append a terminator to the deliberately
#     torn final record in every fixture — the record that pins "a trailing
#     partial line is not a record".
#   - Text normalization can rewrite the raw U+2028 embedded in each fixture,
#     which is the character the framing rule exists to survive.
#
# internal/jsonl and both adapter test suites assert those bytes directly, so a
# rewrite fails the build rather than passing quietly. This entry is the belt.
*.jsonl -text -diff

# Golden renders are compared byte for byte at fixed terminal widths.
internal/hud/testdata/golden/*.txt -text
